<PlainPage
	title="Editorial Policy: How We Test and Review"
	heading="Editorial policy"
	eyebrow="Trust"
	description="How SWG Devo tests settings, scores reviews, keeps guides up to date and handles sponsored content."
	path="/editorial-policy/"
	updated="1 Oct 2026"
>
	<h2>How we test guides</h2>
	<p>
		Every settings guide is tried on at least two devices before it is published, usually one budget and one high-end setup. The patch or version we tested on is shown at the top of the guide.
	</p>
	<h2>How we score reviews</h2>
	<p>
		Reviews are scored out of 10. We play to the credits or for at least 30 hours for open-ended games, and we list the platform, play time and patch with every score. Scores are our own opinion; we never show other sites' ratings as ours.
	</p>
	<h2>Keeping guides current</h2>
	<p>
		When a patch changes something a guide relies on, we update the guide and the "Updated" date. Large changes get a note at the top of the post.
	</p>
	<h2>Sponsored content and links</h2>
	<p>
		Sponsored posts and affiliate links are always labelled. Sponsors never see or approve a review before it is published, and they cannot change a score.
	</p>
	<h2>Corrections</h2>
	<p>Found a mistake? Tell us on Discord or through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and we will fix it and note the change.</p>
</PlainPage>
